{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "framework": "playwright",
  "testId": "testim-migrated/tests/webstore/checkout/verify-order-summary-section-for-retail-user.spec.ts > Webstore - Checkout > verify order summary section for retail user",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "A registered retail user signs in, empties the cart, adds one product of each type (simple, configurable, bundle, grouped; qty 5 each), checks the cart line names and the cart badge (20), checks out with Custom Flat Rate shipping, removes a fixed voucher if present, checks the order-total math and the Purchase Order payment label, and places a COD order.",
    "steps": [
      "Sign in with the dedicated retail account (username/password from the test data) and empty the cart.",
      "For each of the four products: addProductOfAnyType(sku, 5).",
      "Open the cart: productNameLink(id) contains name for each product; cart badge equals totalCartQuantity (20).",
      "Proceed to checkout from the cart.",
      "Select Ship Complete + Custom Flat Rate; remove voucher '1QGSS8ZG6B' if present (hardcoded); Handling Charges; order-total math; PurchaseOrder payment label text.",
      "Select COD, place the order, check the thank-you banner."
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user",
      "product",
      "shipping",
      "payment",
      "cart",
      "order"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "Registered user's cart emptied, then filled with the four products",
      "A new order is placed for the user (COD)"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Each productNameLink(id) contains its name",
      "Cart badge equals '20' (4 products x quantity 5)",
      "Handling Charges label; order total > 0; order-total math within 0.05",
      "paymentLabel(PurchaseOrder) text equals 'PurchaseOrder'; thank-you banner equals thankYouMessage"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Title and the four step labels match the flow.",
      "Credentials (masked) name the existing registered user: USER_WEBSTORE_REGISTERED with preferred.required true (credential source).",
      "tda rows: z-1002656 = PimProductId 933 SimpleProduct; B-100000 = 666 ConfigurableProduct whose line id 532 and name are its default variant z-2510001; z-1234579 = 142 BundleProduct; z-2200003 = 408 GroupedProduct.",
      "Keys: PRODUCT_SIMPLE_IN_STOCK / PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IN_STOCK / PRODUCT_GROUPED_IN_STOCK (sku, productId, name), PRODUCT_CONFIGURABLE_WITH_VARIANTS (parentProductSku, variant1Name; variantAttributes BulbSize,Color,Technology), quantityUsed 5 each.",
      "Missing output: the configurable key returns no productId for the variant line (532).",
      "totalCartQuantity '20' is 4 products x quantity 5 (config arithmetic, not product data): expected-output.",
      "checkoutPage.selectShippingMethod clicks Ship Complete and then lblShippingMethodFLAT (Custom Flat Rate): SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE_ON_STORE, shippingCode FLAT. tda rows: ZnodeShipping FLAT is Custom, DestinationCountryCode US, so countries 'us' (the address itself is masked).",
      "selectCOD/codRadio pays with COD (txtCOD): PAYMENT_COD_ON_STORE. No source carries the COD code the page object uses, so the need has no data source.",
      "MISSING KEY: Purchase Order payment offered on the store to the registered profile; need left out, paymentMethodLabel kept as expected-output.",
      "Data in code: voucher number '1QGSS8ZG6B' is a literal in removeVoucherByNumberIfPresent (line 73), a defensive clean-up (config). Comments at lines 40 and 52 name the SKUs and ids; lines 63-66 are commented-out code.",
      "Profile (atstage 2026-10-31) has no observations for the checkout specs: every source is profiled false. Values were checked read-only with `tda rows` where noted.",
      "Store MaxwellsHardware: the store every migrated webstore spec runs on (as in the approved shopping-cart and PDP entries); not named in the scan.",
      "migrate: the configurable variant's productId (532) has no key output (swap rule 2 fails). The pre-survey flag on totalCartQuantity is not a data dependency (it follows from the quantity), but the strategy is migrate anyway."
    ],
    "confidence": "low",
    "needsReview": true
  },
